<title>FRANCE: French stocks rise on U.S. jobs data.</title>
<headline>French stocks rise on U.S. jobs data.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French stocks rise on rise in U.S. unemployment in June and lower than expected number of new jobs.</p>
<p>Data seen reducing likelihood of interest rate hikes to subdue risk of wage-driven inflation, brokers say.</p>
<p>* CAC-40 index up 30.77 points, or 1.06 pct, at 2,940.22 at 1255 GMT</p>
<p>* CAC-40 July futures contract up 27 points at 2,944</p>
<p>* Volume 4.8 billion francs</p>
